  "summary": "CLI tool with template/test fixtures triggering network and base64 pattern matches",
  "details": "Package is a CLI tool whose shipped files include test fixtures, policy templates, and agent skill scripts. Pattern matches are on: a test file containing example curl commands against hashicorp.com and clearly-placeholder hosts (evil.test, example.com) used as test data; a policy template that references curl/wget/ping as strings in a tool-policy document; and Buffer.from(..., 'base64').toString(...) usages in configuration migration code and release-preparation scripts, which decode configuration or template data rather than executing fetched code. No lifecycle scripts fetch and execute remote content, no hardcoded attacker-controlled C2 endpoint is bound to a network sink, and no reads of installer credential paths (~/.aws, ~/.ssh, ~/.npmrc, browser profiles) are present. The placeholder destinations (evil.test, example.com) are documentation-style stand-ins, not registrable infrastructure.",
